aBc(a){return"Currency conversion unavailable \u2014 P&L vs Cost leaves out a holding with no exchange rate to "+a+" right now."},
ga5L(){return"Shows the total value of your portfolio over time, recorded each day prices are refreshed.\n\n\u2022 Current \u2014 today's total market value of your owned stocks in your display currency\n\u2022 ATH \u2014 the highest portfolio value ever recorded\n\u2022 P&L vs Cost \u2014 your profit with dividends, against what you invested. It is the Portfolio Summary's Total P/L plus every dividend your current holdings have paid \u2014 on the shares you still hold and on shares of them you have sold \u2014 divided by the same Total Invested the Portfolio Summary shows: each buy and sell converted at the exchange rate of its own date where a dated rate exists (where none does, a sell uses the average rate of the holding's buys and anything else today's rate, which the Portfolio Summary then says), and a position that has already paid back more than it cost keeps its surplus in the profit, as on the Summary. Whole portfolio only: N/A under a tag filter, because the curve is never per tag\n\u2022 Value growth \u2014 how much the total value of your portfolio has grown per year, from the first to the latest snapshot. It includes the money you added and took out: a deposit raises it just as a gain would, so it is not your investment return \u2014 the Personal IRR is. Requires at least 90 days of history. Formula: (current / start) ^ (1 / years) \u2212 1\n\n\u2022 Drawdown and Max \u2014 how far below the all-time high you are at each point (0% = at peak, \u221220% = 20% below peak). Like Value growth, this includes money you added or took out: selling shares reads as a drop and buying more as a recovery, so it is not only market moves\n\u2022 Worst drop \u2014 for the single deepest drawdown, roughly how long it took to fall and to recover back to the prior peak (or how long it has been underwater so far). It includes money you added or took out in the same way. Durations are approximate \u2014 snapshots are only recorded on refresh days.\n\nSnapshots are saved automatically on each price refresh, so the curve gets more detailed the longer you use the app.\n\n\u26a0 Tag filter: the chart always shows your full portfolio history \u2014 snapshots are not stored per tag, so the curve cannot be filtered. Value growth is the full portfolio's too, and P&L vs Cost shows N/A while a tag filter is on."},
